course: dictionary
lesson: 11459
title: Admission
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Admission is a noun, and it can mean more than one thing. It can mean being let into a place, as in «admission to the zoo is free for under-fives», or it can mean the money you pay to get in. The words around it show you which meaning is right.
explain: «Admission is 5 dollars» is about money, because you pay that amount to enter. Admission to a hospital is different: it means being taken in as a patient. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence: a price, a place you can enter, or a confession?
explain: Admission can also mean saying that something bad is true, often that you did it. «The boy made an admission: he had broken the window» means he owned up. The phrase «by his own admission» means the person told everyone the truth about themselves.
fact: Admission means being allowed into a place, school or club.
fact: Admission can also mean the money you pay to get in, as in «admission price».
fact: «Admission free» on a sign means you do not have to pay to get in.
fact: An admission is saying that something bad is true, often that you did it.
fact: «By his own admission» means he admitted it himself.
exercise: «Admission to the zoo is free for under-fives.» In this sentence, admission means | A sad story about animals | A ride at the funfair | A zoo keeper's job | *Being allowed into the zoo
exercise: «Admission is 5 dollars per child.» Here, admission means | *The money you pay to get in | An angry letter | Being taken into hospital | A kind of pet
exercise: «The boy made an admission: he had broken the window.» What is an admission here? | Being let into a club | *Saying that something bad is true, often that you did it | A new window | The price of a ticket
test: Sam paid for 2 adults at 8 dollars each and 3 children at 5 dollars each. What is the total admission cost? | 16 dollars | 40 dollars | *31 dollars | 28 dollars
test: «By his own admission, Tom was late.» What does this tell you? | Tom paid the admission charge | Tom was let into the club | The teacher said Tom was late | *Tom admitted it himself
exam: «School admissions open in March, so parents must apply early.» What are school admissions? | A bus timetable | Exams for teachers | The school's football team | *Pupils being allowed to join a school
